; THE RED TANKS. Ground they can drive on, kept off the crests the towers own.
;
; Every bound sits between two numbers measured on THIS pool - the quantiles in
; PlacementRule's header, re-measured for S4 on the post-S3 field:
;   slope 0-14 deg   14.0 sits between p50 13.488 and p75 18.229, so about half
;                    the pool is flat enough. A tank has to be able to drive out
;                    of where it starts, and floor_max_angle 0.9 rad is 51.6 deg
;                    for the body - this is the much tighter "it should not spawn
;                    on a wall" bound, not the physics limit.
;   elevation 0-0.7  a RANK, so it needs no re-deriving when the field changes.
;                    The lower 70%: the glen floor and the mid-slopes, which is
;                    where a patrol is worth meeting. The towers take 0.55-1.0,
;                    so the two groups overlap rather than partition - deliberate,
;                    since a red tank circling a landmark is the good case.
;   openness 0-1     left permissive. Openness here is a 60-unit window on a
;                    2022-unit world (see PlacementRule), so it says "locally
;                    unobstructed" - a fine thing to demand of a landmark and a
;                    meaningless thing to demand of something that drives.
;   edge 0-1         left permissive; edge_margin already holds candidates 6
;                    units inside the world, and any minimum below 0.006 is inert.
;
; separation 150.0 is above the pool's ~100-unit pitch (below that a separation
; cannot reject anything) and above player_keepout 26.0, which is what actually
; matters: the reservation takes the LARGER of the two, so no red tank starts
; within 150 units of the player. With a patrol radius of 110 that still lets a
; patrol circle reach towards the spawn without ever containing it.
;
; ground_clearance 2.0 rather than the tower's 0.6: this is a CharacterBody3D
; with a 3.2 x 4.6 footprint, and a corner of that box dug into a slope is
; resolved by the physics engine launching it. It falls the 2 units in the first
; few frames, exactly as the player's spawn_clearance 4.0 does.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Rule_enemy"]
script = ExtResource("5_rule")
min_slope_degrees = 0.0
max_slope_degrees = 14.0
min_elevation_percentile = 0.0
max_elevation_percentile = 0.7
min_openness = 0.0
max_openness = 1.0
min_edge_fraction = 0.0
max_edge_fraction = 1.0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Group_enemy"]
script = ExtResource("6_group")
id = "enemy"
